    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i ran describe and i don't see any probe failures in the events, just the standard container exited with code 1. it's super weird because the image works fine in dev but fails in this gke cluster. could it be something with the way the nodes are attaching storage or an issue with the container runtime itself? i'm trying to figure out if there's some hidden config mismatch between the k8s manifest and how the node actually handles the container.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Since the error is a fatal module not found (`code 1`) and not reported by the probe, it's strongly pointing back to an environment or path issue, not the runtime itself. Double-check if any PersistentVolumeClaims (PVCs) or ConfigMaps are mounted into the pod and if those mounts are shadowing or causing conflicts with the application's expected `/app` directory. Compare the *exact* runtime environment variables passed to the pod in GKE against what you are using locally to catch subtle differences.",
      "source": "target",
